/*
 * Explicit compound-type cast validation.
 *
 * CastExplicitCompoundValidation performs semantic validation of explicit
 * casts involving compound types. It is responsible for:
 *
 *   - validating explicit casts to option types,
 *   - validating explicit casts to pointer types,
 *   - reconstructing compound values with rewritten inner values,
 *   - enforcing memory-ownership rules for pointer casts,
 *   - propagating detailed diagnostics when explicit casts fail.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::value::operator::cast_::explicit::compound
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/value/operator/cast_/explicit/compound.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-06-14
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
